{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `at()` returns −1 for missing lines, so `lessThan` can pass on absence**

`int at(String line) => lines.indexOf(line);` yields −1 when an expected profile line is missing, and the first two assertions use `lessThan` — so if `(deny file-write* (subpath "/etc"))` were dropped from emission, `at(...) == -1` is `lessThan` any real index and the test passes on the exact regression it guards. The sibling test in this group guards with `greaterThanOrEqualTo(0)` first; do the same here (or make `at` throw/expect non-negative) so a missing line can never satisfy an ordering check:

```dart
int at(String line) {
  final i = lines.indexOf(line);
  expect(i, greaterThanOrEqualTo(0), reason: 'missing profile line: $line');
  return i;
