{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `CubeToolPolicy(allow: {'head', 'printf'})` is dead config here**

`MacOsSandboxBackend.buildSandboxProfile` emits only filesystem/network rules — the tool allowlist is enforced by `SandboxedShell`/`CubePolicyEngine`, which this test bypasses (it wraps commands via `wrapCommand` directly). As written, the spec implies `head`/`printf` are gated by the profile when nothing checks them; any binary would run. Either drop the `tools:` entry or add a comment that it is documentary only, so future readers do not model new live tests on a non-existent enforcement layer.
